{"id":"lesbos","name":"Lesbos","qid":"Q128087","country":"Greece","locality":"North Aegean Region, Lesbos Regional Unit","lat":"39.21","lon":"26.28","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Natural formations","period":"","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"","type":"island","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lesbos","text":"Lesbos or Lesvos (Greek: Λέσβος, romanized: Lésvos [ˈlezvos]) is a Greek island located in the northeastern Aegean Sea. It has an area of 1,633 km2 (631 sq mi), with approximately 400 km (249 mi) of coastline, making it the third largest island in Greece and the eighth largest in the Mediterranean. It is separated from Asia Minor by the narrow Mytilini Strait.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lesbos","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-34972bbd5630","w":1200,"h":1189,"title":"Lesvos.jpg","o":"gh-34972bbd5630.jpg","credit":{"text":"http://eol.jsc.nasa.gov/","license":"Public domain","license_url":"","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lesvos.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"assassins-creed-odyssey--lesbos","game":"assassins-creed-odyssey","name":"Lesbos","verified":false,"text":"Lesbos is a Greek island in the northeast Aegean Sea that is most famous for being the home of lyric poet Sappho. Together with Chios, Lesbos formed the Petrified Islands.","text_source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Lesbos","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-e179fa06b2d7","w":1200,"h":549,"o":"gh-e179fa06b2d7.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Odyssey, © Ubisoft Quebec.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File:ACOD_Lesbos_-_Concept_Art.jpg","via":"Fandom (assassinscreed)","note":"Fandom upload by Lady Kyashira on 2020-06-12"}},{"id":"gh-p02b4f36eb66","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-p02b4f36eb66.jpg","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Odyssey, © Ubisoft Quebec.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File: