dit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Odyssey, © Ubisoft Quebec.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File:ACOd-Lesbos-SeasideCavern.jpg","via":"Fandom (assassinscreed)","note":"Fandom upload by Sadelyrate on 2019-10-13"}}]},{"id":"assassins-creed-odyssey--petrified-islands","game":"assassins-creed-odyssey","name":"Petrified Islands","verified":false,"text":"The Petrified Islands is a name used for the group of Greek islands in the northeastern Aegean Sea. They included both Lesbos and Chios. It was home to the poet Sappho, and contained the city of Mytilene, which rebelled against Athens at one point, resulting in its subjugation.","text_source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Petrified_Islands","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-pb533a479d6a","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-pb533a479d6a.jpg","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Odyssey, © Ubisoft Quebec.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File:ACOd-PetrifiedIslands-Lesbos-east.jpg","via":"Fandom (assassinscreed)","note":"Fandom upload by Sadelyrate on 2019-09-29"}}]}]}